        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "2fa8e8ae-a4bf-5a13-a343-470bb6c728e8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jean-Philippe Rameau, Voltaire, Charles Dill, Giacomo Puccini, Henri Larrivée\n- Works: Castor et Pollux, Samson, Manon Lescaut\n- Topics: opera composition, revivals, aesthetics\n\nFacts:\n- Charles Dill proposes that Jean-Philippe Rameau composed Castor et Pollux in 1737 just after working with Voltaire on the unfinished opera Samson.\n- Charles Dill states that Jean-Philippe Rameau used Voltaire's aesthetics in Castor et Pollux.\n- In 1755, Henri Larrivée made his first solo appearance as a high priest in a revival of Jean-Philippe Rameau's Castor et Pollux.\n- Giacomo Puccini composed Manon Lescaut, a four-act opera, between 1890 and 1893.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "df7a4ecd-7187-5b15-b046-aabdc9187052",
